Fire Base Setuo Steps: 
Step 1: Create Firebase Project

Go to Firebase Console
Click "Add project"
Enter project name: "Expense Manager"
Follow the setup wizard

Step 2: Register Android App

In Firebase Console, click on Android icon
Enter your package name: com.example.expensemanager
Enter app nickname (optional): "Expense Manager"
Download google-services.json
Place the file in app/ directory of your Android project

Step 3: Enable Firebase Authentication

In Firebase Console, go to Authentication
Click "Get Started"
Enable Email/Password sign-in method
Click "Enable" and save

Step 4: Set Up Firebase Realtime Database

In Firebase Console, go to Realtime Database
Click "Create Database"
Choose location (closest to your users)
Start in Test Mode (for development)
Update rules later for production:

json{
  "rules": {
    "users": {
      "$uid": {
        ".read": "$uid === auth.uid",
        ".write": "$uid === auth.uid"
      }
    },
    "expenses": {
      "$uid": {
        ".read": "$uid === auth.uid",
        ".write": "$uid === auth.uid",
        ".indexOn": ["timestamp", "date"]
      }
    }
  }
}
Step 5: Database Structure
Your Firebase Realtime Database will have this structure:
expense-manager-db/
├── users/
│   └── {userId}/
│       ├── userId: "string"
│       ├── fullName: "string"
│       ├── email: "string"
│       ├── monthlyBudget: number
│       └── profileImageUrl: "string"
│
└── expenses/
    └── {userId}/
        └── {expenseId}/
            ├── expenseId: "string"
            ├── userId: "string"
            ├── amount: number
            ├── category: "string"
            ├── date: "string" (DD-MM-YYYY)
            ├── note: "string"
            └── timestamp: number
Step 6: Add Dependencies
Make sure your build.gradle files are configured correctly (already provided in the project files).
Step 7: Sync and Build

Sync your project with Gradle files
Build the project
Run on emulator or physical device

Security Rules for Production
For production, update your Firebase Realtime Database rules:
json{
  "rules": {
    "users": {
      "$uid": {
        ".read": "$uid === auth.uid",
        ".write": "$uid === auth.uid",
        ".validate": "newData.hasChildren(['userId', 'fullName', 'email'])"
      }
    },
    "expenses": {
      "$uid": {
        ".read": "$uid === auth.uid",
        ".write": "$uid === auth.uid",
        "$expenseId": {
          ".validate": "newData.hasChildren(['expenseId', 'userId', 'amount', 'category', 'date', 'timestamp'])"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
Troubleshooting
Common Issues:

Google Services Error: Make sure google-services.json is in the correct location (app/ folder)
Authentication Error: Verify Email/Password is enabled in Firebase Console
Database Permission Denied: Check your database rules are set correctly
Build Errors: Ensure all dependencies are properly synced
Check dashboard for budget overview
